{"id": "EUVD-2026-86859", "enisaUuid": "ba0eebca-c7fc-3b29-b397-ddedd60e9895", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: initialise args->total for parent pointer updates\n\nxfs_parent_da_args_init() builds an xfs_da_args from a zeroed\nxfs_parent_args (kmem_cache_zalloc), leaving args->total == 0.\nxfs_da_grow_inode_int() treats that field as a running block reservation\nand subtracts from it; because it is an xfs_extlen_t (uint32_t), the\nfirst attr-fork growth wraps it to ~0U.  That defeats the free-space\ncheck in xfs_alloc_space_available(), and when it coincides with an AG\nthat has exactly zero available blocks the allocation is clamped to\nmaxlen 0 and returns -ENOSPC, which xfs_defer_finish_noroll() escalates\nto a filesystem shutdown.\n\nSet args->total the way the log recovery path does\n(xfs_attri_recover_work(), xfs_attr_item.c:706), in the add and replace\npaths that can grow the fork.  Removals and lookups never grow it, so\nthey leave the field alone, matching that switch.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ad85bce62cadfdf4242f6e6bbff2a52e51d30f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c66e138af626cad4210da449996ae9e07ee63add", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac9032882d673dd6679e1d873a2dc0131a1aeb43", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e4ebb6afaa34bd2e8ce52da231003d24111c2d6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hph3-hwfc-67wh", "CVE-2026-97551"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16e9743d-bdee-3db3-b1f3-431ff1045df5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7c62d90c12c6cc86f10b8a62cefe0029374b6ff <c66e138af626cad4210da449996ae9e07ee63add"}, {"id": "2389cc0a-7c6f-3277-a703-1c4b9ed9d48c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "314fd9f1-7f34-3ba3-a161-90d8438dae61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3cb5d0b0-9075-3add-a5a1-2e6cd031af38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "3ff4bce3-d941-3bc3-9847-f6e67b68ff93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7c62d90c12c6cc86f10b8a62cefe0029374b6ff <8e4ebb6afaa34bd2e8ce52da231003d24111c2d6"}, {"id": "42e73060-78f3-392a-9ad6-cd5e782fa87b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6ba73740-e55c-38c3-b441-4c09fb9e4b9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7c62d90c12c6cc86f10b8a62cefe0029374b6ff <ac9032882d673dd6679e1d873a2dc0131a1aeb43"}, {"id": "78baecc5-e06c-3e99-9fbe-d7bf67b06901", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "86316fb8-e99c-38f3-88d7-8f08dc8ef59f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7c62d90c12c6cc86f10b8a62cefe0029374b6ff <9ad85bce62cadfdf4242f6e6bbff2a52e51d30f1"}, {"id": "9d5cae0d-e19a-3184-ae48-ccfc0a7bea9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9c3c4a58-e983-3f91-8690-e732caa16795", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}